-The FFN has three selectable formulations (module flags, mutually exclusive):
+The FFN has four selectable formulations (module flags, mutually exclusive):
+
+  * ``_MOE_ASGEMM_ONDEVICE`` -- the full dense all-expert FFN is expressed as
+    one activation-stationary compiler contract.  One ``[T,H]`` activation is
+    retained across a static expert loop; prepacked gate, up, and down expert
+    banks advance once per iteration; runtime ``[E,T,1]`` route weights are
+    applied after down; and one ``[T,H]`` accumulator is returned.  This is the
+    compiler-integrated successor to the chunked Step-2 formulation below.
 
   * ``_MOE_CHUNKED_ONDEVICE`` (Gate-A5-PROVEN, mean_rel=0.028) -- the WHOLE FFN
     runs on the device; host does only chunk-loop glue. Sidesteps the routing
@@ -66,6 +73,9 @@ split / loop bmm paths -- the chunked path uses plain 2D matmuls):
 
 import torch
 import torch.nn.functional as F
+from torch_spyre._inductor import config as spyre_config
+from torch_spyre._inductor import spyre_hint
